On 7/1/07, Jon Top Hat Jones <eyeonus@gmail.com> wrote:
>
> Also, my personal preference for things like trimester and such would be to
> not use a lujvo, and instead use either {ci lo masti} or {lo ci masti},
> whichever of "3 of a month-span" or "a 3 month-span" is better.

{masti be li ci} is "3-month span".

{ci lo masti} and {lo ci masti} are three (one)-month spans, which
may be independen of one another.

> On a semi-related note, which of those is equivalent to {ci masti}?

{ci lo masti}, as they are both {ci da}.

{ci da broda} can always be expanded to some long formula that
comes down to there being three and only three different things
da, de and di, such that {da broda ije de broda ije di broda}.

